<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bernard I of Armagnac</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">10th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Bernard the Squinter, Bernard le Louche</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bernard I, called the Squinter, was the first count of Armagnac in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gascony">Gascony</a>, a member of the ruling house of the counts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fezensac">Fezensac</a>. Around 960 Armagnac was separated as his share of the family lands. His descendants ruled the hill country around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/auch">Auch</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lectoure">Lectoure</a>, and the house of Armagnac later became one of the most powerful noble families of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>.</p></div>
